  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Ledger",
    "overview": "A single control screen that reads like a well-kept notebook page in Eido's language: warm cream paper, brown ink, one big number. The palette, the Outfit typeface and the 28dp card silhouette are inherited from the author's other app, Eido (palette source: `Eido/packages/ui-core/components/gluestack-ui-provider/config.ts`, light and dark modes); each Android color resource carries a comment naming the Eido scale step it came from (e.g. `bg` = background-900, `ink` = primary-0). New surfaces should keep that lineage rather than drift toward Material defaults.\n\nThe screen is flat and tonal. Content sits on cream, grouped into soft-cornered surface cards; hierarchy comes from size and ink weight, not from color or depth. Color carries meaning only for state: green when protection runs, orange when it is cut, with the setup card tinting warm when action is needed. Everything else is a brown-on-cream ramp. The voice is French, sentence case, short.\n\nDensity is relaxed: generous 24dp card insets, 64-76dp row heights, 32dp breathing room above section labels. The one moment of motion that carries meaning is the counter climbing from the last-seen value.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Eido lineage: cream paper, brown ink, Outfit, 28dp cards.",
      "Flat tonal layering; no shadows anywhere.",
      "One display number per screen, tabular figures.",
      "Green/orange reserved for state.",
      "Full light and dark parity through `values` / `values-night` resources."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State-Only Color Rule",
        "body": "Green and orange appear only as status signals (an 8dp dot, the setup card wash). Never as decoration, buttons, or links.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Eido Provenance Rule",
        "body": "Every color is a named step of Eido's gluestack palette; add new colors by taking the next Eido step, with a comment naming it, never by inventing a hex.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase, no letterspaced labels. Section labels are plain sentence-case 14sp Medium in Umber.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Number Rule",
        "body": "Any changing number (counter, timestamps) uses `tnum` so values do not jitter as they animate or align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper-Flat Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces separate by tone, never by shadow. If a new layer is needed, take the next Eido step.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every new color from Eido's palette and note the step it maps to, in both `values` and `values-night`.",
      "**Do** group content in Linen cards with 28dp corners and 24dp insets.",
      "**Do** keep one 72sp tabular number as the screen's focal point.",
      "**Do** keep touch targets at 48dp minimum even when the visual control is smaller.",
      "**Do** dim and disable (45%) content that cannot work yet, and lead with the card that fixes it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add shadows or elevation; separate layers by tone.",
      "**Don't** use green or orange outside status signals.",
      "**Don't** use uppercase or tracked-out labels.",
      "**Don't** reach for the purple wellbeing look or progress rings; this is a calm control screen, not a wellness tracker.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second typeface for display; Outfit carries all roles."
    ]
  }
}